impact:
An attacker controls a live `playticorp.com` origin with a valid certificate. That is enough to:

- host credential-phishing pages that carry the Playtika brand and a genuine Playtika domain, which
  survives most link-reputation and brand controls;
- run an OAuth/SSO redirect or `postMessage` target on an origin the parent domain trusts;
- receive and harvest any cookie, bearer token or `Referer` still addressed to the hostname — the name
  `shm-playground` suggests staging/shared tooling, which is often wired into internal portals;
- poison cached or pre-generated links to the host.
